# Web Lesson 38 -- internal hom and cartesian-closed boundary.
# visual: svg
# loops: 0
# ***************************************************************************
# * PREREQUISITES -- products, exponentials, evaluation, beta, and eta.
# * CATEGORICAL SETTING -- one displayed two-point object pair in finite Set.
# * LAW / UNIVERSAL PROPERTY -- internal hom for one pair; global element from 1.
# * BOUNDARY -- cartesian closure requires products/exponentials for every pair.
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS
# * Local evidence passes while a missing pair blocks the category-wide claim.
# ***************************************************************************
;
include "lib/finite_exponentials.mlpl"  # reuse pair-level exponential evidence
function_rows = [[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]]  # finite internal hom object
pair_certificate = u:bounded_pair_has_internal_hom(1, u:two_point_exponential_is_complete(function_rows), 1, 1)  # CT072
selected_global_element = u:global_element_selects_internal_hom_row(function_rows, 2)  # CT073 singleton map
category_wide_certificate = u:displayed_pairs_support_cartesian_closure([1, 0])  # CT071 coverage fails
missing_pair_witness = 1 - category_wide_certificate  # COUNTEREXAMPLE to overgeneralization
disp(selected_global_element)
disp([pair_certificate, category_wide_certificate, missing_pair_witness])
# ***************************************************************************
# * THE VISUAL
# * Read local internal hom, singleton selection, then the missing every-pair box.
# ***************************************************************************
def u:cartesian_closed_boundary_web_visual() {
  "Render local internal-hom evidence and the missing category-wide coverage witness.";
  u:cartesian_closed_boundary_visual()
}  # narrated shared visual entry point
cartesian_closed_boundary_visual = u:cartesian_closed_boundary_web_visual()  # bind visual constant
cartesian_closed_boundary_visual  # display bound visual once
# ***************************************************************************
# * HOW TO READ THE RESULT
# * Top passes for one pair; the singleton chooses f2; bottom leaves one pair open.
# * The dashed path is not a failed exponential—it is missing universal coverage.
# * THE POINT -- cartesian closure quantifies over every object pair.
# ***************************************************************************
